Independent exact-head review — bounded source/test acceptance (COMMENT, not release approval)

Reviewed PR head `5b09019aa684f0f06c077335e118b854cf3b89fa` against base `48dce8f697825c8cd5f99b3e5aeea3953647f8c2`. The exact three-file scope and Git blob hashes were re-fetched; runtime blob `a97af941a0313808f3d71b8c3b9428d5108a18f7`, test blob `5b41d822dd9942c57c51cff4c1ef52a35738277a`.

Node v24.19.0:
- exact committed focused suite: 8/8 pass;
- unchanged base substituted under the same tests: 2 pass / 6 fail, reproducing the defect;
- independent held-outs: 1,218/1,218 assertions pass across server and serialized VM factories;
- exact PR431/PR488 consumer modules plus forecast dependency and focused suite: 25/25 pass, zero skips/failures.

Held-outs covered holes/inherited/accessor factors without getter execution, custom traversal, cross-realm/frozen/sealed/null-prototype/subclass arrays, length bounds, invalid/extreme numbers, rounding, transparent/revoked/throwing proxies and valid-input differential cases. No Critical, Important or Minor blocking finding was found within the documented trusted same-realm input boundary.

Boundary: arbitrary hostile Proxy isolation is explicitly not provided; a descriptor-fabricating proxy can still substitute evidence. The existing archive/composer suite was not independently run because the exact binary blob could not be decoded by the connector and no validated local archive was available. Supported Node 22.23.2, installed-image, canonical integration, hosted and customer proof remain required.

Verdict: SOURCE/TEST ACCEPTED for this isolated repair only. Not merge, deployment, payroll authority or customer-proof approval.
